WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:03.659
Are you a brand designer looking
to learn and improve your brand identity and

00:00:03.659 --> 00:00:09.910
packaging design workflow and skills to have
a less stressful life, and to attract better-paying

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:10.910
clients?

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.410
If yes, then perfect, I got your back!

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:19.350
Today I’ll share with you my easy to follow
6 steps process to design from scratch a

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:24.560
brand identity and packaging design for this
sassy chewing gum brand, so that you’ll

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:30.859
be able to design professional, on-brief,
eye-catching and fully functional deliverables

00:00:30.859 --> 00:00:32.480
for your clients!

00:00:36.003 --> 00:00:37.004
Hello guys!

00:00:37.004 --> 00:00:41.530
My name is Loredana, and I am a freelance
digital illustrator and graphic designer with

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:47.750
a focus on playful brand identity and packaging
design services for ambitious small businesses

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:49.190
targeting female customers!

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:54.790
Today I’ll show you how I structure and
create from scratch a brand identity and packaging

00:00:54.790 --> 00:01:00.500
design for a chewing gum brand, making sure
the brand and its product will truly stand

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:01.640
out among competitors.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:06.100
So, let’s dive right into my 6 steps design
process, and have some fun!

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.990
But first, let’s meet the brand and the
design brief!

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:13.840
Chumble is a playful &amp; sassy sugar-free chewing
gum brand with 2 exploding fun flavours, Citrus

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.470
&amp; Tropical, that unlike any other gum keep
up to 3 hours.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:18.610
Tagline: Mind your own CHUMBLE!

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:21.220
Slogan: 3 hours of UNSERIOUS flavours!

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:25.680
Brand Values &amp; Adjectives: natural &amp; fun flavours,
long-lasting, customer-oriented, healthy teeth

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:29.990
&amp; fresh breath, playful, modern with a touch
of retro, feminine, friendly, approachable,

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:32.100
casual, bold, energetic, cool.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:37.390
Target Customer: 18-35 years old women, sassy,
modern, playful, energetic, active unconventional,

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:40.720
funny, women who take good care of their teeth.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:44.810
Brand Focus &amp; Design Objectives: To create
a full brand visual identity and packaging

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:48.342
design that help the brand stand out among
competitors on the market shelves.

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:54.240
Before jumping into the creative phase, and
even before putting together the creative

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.200
direction and mood board for your project,
you must do competitor research to know what

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.520
to avoid design-wise!

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.979
You must religiously follow the design brief,
and as you remember, Chumble’s design objective

00:02:03.979 --> 00:02:08.789
is to design a brand identity and packaging
that make the brand stand out among competitors.

00:02:08.789 --> 00:02:12.920
Also, a thorough brand discovery phase, with
in-depth questionnaires to discover your client's

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:16.260
needs and objectives help you to create a
strategic design.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.870
Identify your client’s top brand competitors'
aesthetic and mission!

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:24.010
For Chumble the competitors are Hubba Bubba,
Bubblicious and Big Babol, but as their brands

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:27.620
are way to playful and aimed at children,
while Chumble targets sassy Millenial and

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.280
Gen Z women, I completely avoid their aesthetic.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:34.310
If you’re struggling with putting a mood
board together for a visual identity and packaging

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:38.810
design project, make sure you include photos
related to the business, colour palettes,

00:02:38.810 --> 00:02:41.510
clear font styles, and clear illustration
style.

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:45.700
This way the client will have a clear idea
of your creative direction for the project!

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:46.700
Hot Pinterest Tip!

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:51.338
Pin your visual inspiration for creative direction
on a secret board, to keep your project private!

00:02:54.069 --> 00:02:57.340
Also in this stage, the answers from the brand
discovery questionnaires will help you sketch

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.180
strategic concept designs.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:03.300
After drawing as many rough concept sketches
as needed, you chose the most adapted idea

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:07.380
for your client’s needs and objectives,
always having in mind their target customer

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:08.380
demographics!

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:12.770
Hot Design Tip: Always draw your sketches
in black to focus on the concept and start

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:15.028
with simple, rough concept sketches!

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:20.780
Get ready for a typefaces and fonts hunt!

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:25.180
When choosing and pairing typefaces and fonts
for your brand and packaging design projects,

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:30.709
always have in mind the design brief, the
brand’s personality, and the target customer.

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:33.300
Typography can really make or break a brand
identity.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:37.770
Each typeface and font have their own personality
and style, conveyed through lines, shapes

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:42.819
and corners, so pick those matching the brand’s
personality, while targeting the psychology

00:03:42.819 --> 00:03:44.860
of its intended customers.

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:49.650
You must choose between serifs, sans serifs,
slab serifs, scripts…

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:53.530
Font pairing is not an easy task, as fonts
must complement each other while reflecting

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:55.480
the brand’s look and feel!

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:59.319
When in doubt, return to the design brief
and the brand questionnaires; you’ll find

00:03:59.319 --> 00:04:01.750
there all the answers you need!

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:05.819
In my opinion, the best typefaces you can
choose are those with glyphs, as they are

00:04:05.819 --> 00:04:07.090
extremely practical.

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:11.750
It’s always good to have more letter options
when creating a brand identity, you’ll never

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:14.580
know which one better suits the brand’s
personality!

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:19.509
There are many places where you can find also
free typefaces and fonts for personal and

00:04:19.509 --> 00:04:23.889
commercial use, and one of these places is
Google Fonts, which I picked for this personal

00:04:23.889 --> 00:04:25.749
project.

00:04:25.749 --> 00:04:31.139
I strongly advise you to customise all the
typefaces and fonts when crafting logo variations!

00:04:31.139 --> 00:04:36.009
This way you can tailor each letter to perfectly
fit and emphasize the brand’s unique identity!

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:42.589
For Chumble I chose three typefaces, a super
contemporary and cool sans serif for the wordmark,

00:04:42.589 --> 00:04:47.840
a simple sans serif for the body copy, and
a playful and bubbly sans serif for the tagline and

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:53.026
flavour, script-like, to create a nice contrast
while having in mind the product niche.

00:04:54.779 --> 00:04:55.990
Hot Design Tip!

00:04:55.990 --> 00:05:00.360
Before expanding typography in Adobe Illustrator,
make sure you save a copy of your editable

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:02.002
type box as a backup!

00:05:03.479 --> 00:05:06.729
Because typography is such a rich topic, I
promise you I’ll dedicate a future video

00:05:06.729 --> 00:05:07.274
to it!

00:05:09.289 --> 00:05:13.319
Creating logo variations takes time and patience,
trials, and errors, but it’s such a fun

00:05:13.319 --> 00:05:16.330
and creative process, and the result worth’s
every second!

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:21.869
For my clients, I create 4 logo variations:
a primary logo, a secondary logo, a logomark

00:05:21.869 --> 00:05:25.025
and a submark logo or a lettermark.

00:05:25.279 --> 00:05:28.870
Every brand designer has his own way of presenting
the brand identity to the client.

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:33.360
I do one concept method, which means presenting
one logo concept and its variations, one packaging

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:36.940
design concept and its variations etc to the
client.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:40.949
After finishing the design and illustration
in vector, you present your client only the

00:05:40.949 --> 00:05:45.409
best concept, and based on the received feedback
you perfect your final design.

00:05:45.409 --> 00:05:49.180
This way the clients will not be overwhelmed
with responsibility, and in plus, you are

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:52.460
the brand designer, you are the expert in
matter, and you should know what works best

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:53.460
for the brand!

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:57.210
For example, for Chumble the final concept
was the third one, even though it was just

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:58.710
a personal project!

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:02.211
In this stage, I’ve already added this playful
brand colour palette and I am copying and

00:06:02.211 --> 00:06:06.490
pasting artboards to create the colour variations
for all Chumble brand logos!

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:11.760
Show your support by giving a like and pressing
subscribe to my channel for more playful illustration

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:16.360
and graphic design tips for freelancers and
small business owners!

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:21.389
In my case, the entire creative direction
is built around the values of Chumble, envisioning

00:06:21.389 --> 00:06:26.059
a fresh, modern with a touch of retro, playful
and sassy brand for sassy women.

00:06:26.059 --> 00:06:30.930
Thus, the brand colours I chose are fun, vibrant,
youthful, and fresh, being inspired by Chumble’s

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:31.930
chewing gum flavours.

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:36.510
I must admit, I had a bit of work until ending
fully satisfied with the final concept for

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:39.619
Chumble’s logo variations, but I am glad I did.

00:06:39.619 --> 00:06:44.809
This negative space logo totally emphasizes
the brand, its product, and its target customers,

00:06:44.809 --> 00:06:45.949
all in a single mark.

00:06:45.949 --> 00:06:48.869
In on brief, and in plus is clever.

00:06:48.869 --> 00:06:50.210
And this is always a point-in plus!

00:06:50.210 --> 00:06:51.344
Hot Design Tip! When designing a brand identity, stay away
from RGB color profile!

00:06:51.344 --> 00:06:52.546
Instead, design in CMYK and, to be an absolute
pro, pull out those Pantone color book!

00:06:52.546 --> 00:06:56.069
Personally, this is my second favourite step
in the process.

00:06:56.069 --> 00:06:58.389
Stay tuned to discover which is number one!

00:06:58.389 --> 00:07:02.249
For each fun flavour, I’ve created a different
design, illustration, and colour palette,

00:07:02.249 --> 00:07:07.369
to differentiate its uniqueness, and I adapted
the composition and text content for two types

00:07:07.369 --> 00:07:09.610
of packaging.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:14.770
The brand pattern and illustrations for packaging
are inspired by Pin-up sassy models, as the

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:18.349
style is perfect for the playful and feminine
personality of the brand.

00:07:18.349 --> 00:07:22.879
As you can see, to vectorize the character
illustrations created in Procreate, I used

00:07:22.879 --> 00:07:27.189
the mighty Image Trace in Adobe Illustrator,
choosing the Silhouettes option.

00:07:27.189 --> 00:07:31.939
If you don’t know, Image trace allows you
to convert raster images to vector artwork,

00:07:31.939 --> 00:07:35.979
so that you’ll be able to integrate your
custom hand-drawn sketches and illustrations

00:07:35.979 --> 00:07:38.520
into the brand identity project.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:43.629
And this is simply fantastic, especially for
creating illustrative logos and organic illustrations

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:46.879
for packaging, stationary and print in general.

00:07:46.879 --> 00:07:51.849
This option is perfect for those creatives
who love drawing, both digital and traditional,

00:07:51.849 --> 00:07:53.529
and are looking for an organic style.

00:07:53.529 --> 00:07:57.599
Please don’t ever use this tool to trace
other people’s hard work!

00:07:57.599 --> 00:08:02.939
While designing the packaging, my two Pinup
characters depicting the brand flavours – Tropical

00:08:02.939 --> 00:08:06.499
and Citrus, suffered a couple of changes,
better said improvements.

00:08:06.499 --> 00:08:11.849
All these to make sure the brand and its product
will truly stand out among competitors!

00:08:13.693 --> 00:08:18.389
I prefer drawing the illustrations in Procreate,
because is perfect, especially for those textured

00:08:18.389 --> 00:08:19.479
brushes.

00:08:19.479 --> 00:08:23.003
And in plus, the Apple pencil is priceless.

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:29.289
After final changes and tweaks in Illustrator
I began the brand colour exploration for the

00:08:29.289 --> 00:08:33.346
packaging until I found the perfect colours
for each product flavour.

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:39.331
The Pinup characters I’ve drawn for the
packaging are also the stars of the brand

00:08:39.331 --> 00:08:40.460
patterns.

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:45.550
When creating brand identity, brand patterns
are extremely useful for packaging design,

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:50.581
social media, and web use, stationary because
they reflect the brand’s personality in

00:08:50.581 --> 00:08:52.031
such an effective visual way.

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:05.130
A dieline is a digital file of your packaging
template used to show the proper layout of

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:06.005
the finished product.

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:12.090
Dielines are helpful for figuring out the
best placement of your brand design elements

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:17.150
and act as diagrams for your packaging template
that printers will use as a reference when

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:20.460
developing the hard prototypes of the product
packaging.

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:24.120
Usually, you’ll receive one from the client,
but you can also find them online, download

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:25.425
and use them for your projects.

00:10:28.450 --> 00:10:31.764
When designing packaging, ask the client to
give you all the text information you need

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:36.710
to include on the packaging, the ingredients,
nutrition facts, the barcode etc.

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:41.490
As always, pay attention to hierarchy, legibility,
and all the other design principles.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:46.520
Design a packaging for a product thinking
especially about its target customer and his

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:50.130
experience when interacting with the product
and the brand!

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:54.310
You should ask yourself: What does the customer
see first on the packaging?

00:10:54.310 --> 00:10:56.010
What does he see second?

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:57.470
But third?

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:00.026
Where will the product be placed on the market
shelves?

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:07.460
Hot Design Tip: When designing typography
for packaging design, don’t go under 5 points,

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:10.003
otherwise it would be hard to read by customers!

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:39.200
Mockups are suuuper important!

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:43.320
You have no idea how much they help you in
the brand identity and packaging presentation

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:47.840
that you’ll prepare for your client, to
portray the brand in a realistic manner, sell

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:52.870
your concept design, and especially convince
him that it’s the perfect one for the brand!

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:57.400
You can find plenty of free mockups online,
for a multitude of purposes and industries,

00:11:57.400 --> 00:12:01.820
so take your time, seriously take your time,
and search for the best of the best for your

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:02.820
project.

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:07.800
Don’t worry if you are not 100% satisfied
with what you find, you can edit their Psd

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:11.010
files however your creative direction requires
for the project!

00:12:11.010 --> 00:12:15.630
I like to completely manipulate and transform
them in Adobe Photoshop to create an immersive

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:18.720
brand experience, look and feel for the client.

00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:22.450
Your mockup designs must shout the brand’s
personality and mission while targeting the

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:24.550
ideal customer’s psychology.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:29.749
They should show the client how he can correctly
use in real life the brand designs you created.

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:35.070
Hot Design Tip: If you are not very proficient
in Adobe Photoshop yet, learn it!

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:39.430
You have no idea how useful and powerful it
is when creating, editing, and compositing

00:12:39.430 --> 00:12:42.028
realistic mockups and photos for your projects!

00:12:48.034 --> 00:12:49.001
In this last step,

00:12:56.142 --> 00:13:00.920
you must test the usability
of your packaging design and see how it looks like in real life.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:04.600
This is the only way you’ll be sure that
the chosen typography keeps its legibility,

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:09.010
the colours print well, that your design is
on point and ready to rock!

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:12.561
Now is the perfect moment to check and fix
your design flaws, before sending the brand

00:13:12.561 --> 00:13:15.640
identity and packaging design presentation
to your client!

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:19.310
And lastly, we’ve arrived at my favourite
step in absolute – prototyping!

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:23.940
Print your designs at home and don’t worry,
you don’t need a fancy printer and special

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:28.880
paper or cardboard, you just need to test
their usability for future customers.

00:13:28.880 --> 00:13:33.110
For this step, you’ll need also scissors
or a paper guillotine, paper glue and a bit

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:36.240
of patience to hand-craft your packaging variations!

00:13:36.240 --> 00:13:40.820
Snip, snip, enjoy this relaxing process, and
don’t forget to take some cool packaging

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:44.023
photos for your brand identity presentation
and social media.

00:15:33.032 --> 00:15:38.530
Are you ready to finally meet the brand-new
visual identity and packaging of Chumble?

00:15:38.530 --> 00:15:45.240
But first, I want to thank you for watching
and I hope my 6 steps design process will

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:48.650
help you improve your workflow and life!

00:15:48.650 --> 00:15:54.760
Show your support by giving a like and pressing
subscribe to my channel for more digital illustration

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:59.024
and graphic design tips for freelancers and
small business owners!

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:06.750
Ladies and Gentlemen, mind your own Chumble
and enjoy your 3 hours of unserious flavours!

